  "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen `username` or `password` are passed as bytes to `HTTPDigestAuth`, the f-string formatting in `build_digest_header` produces Python `bytes.__repr__` (e.g. `b'...'`) in the Digest header instead of the actual credential value.\n\nExample: `HTTPDigestAuth('Ondřej'.encode('utf-8'), 'heslíčko')` produces `Digest username=\"b'Ond\\\\xc5\\\\99ej'\"` which is incorrect.\n\n## Fix\n\nNormalize bytes to str (via UTF-8 decode) at the start of `build_digest_header`. This ensures:\n1. The Digest header `username` field contains the correct string value\n2. The digest hash computation (A1 = username:realm:password) uses the correct values\n3. Both str and bytes inputs work correctly\n\n## Changes\n- 14 lines added, 2 lines changed in `src/requests/auth.py`\n- No new dependencies, no API changes\n\nFixes #6102",
